Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le16ob08re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Living the Dream", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Recommendation Letter", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Writes well organized texts about the application for a job in an international organization through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Writes well organized texts about the application for a job in an international organization through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "  Writes well organized texts about the application for a job in an international organization through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Writes well organized texts about the application for a job in an international organization through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Writes well organized texts about the application for a job in an international organization through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Did you apply there? Oh, then I'll apply there too.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Be going to</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm going to write a reference letter for my cousin.</span> <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">My former boss isn't going to write me a reference letter.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm leaving my interview now.</span> <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm interviewing for a job at 2 p.m. tomorrow.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It starts at 11:00 a.m.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " They are going to need just a little information about what I did for you as an intern at Polygon. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They are also going to want to know some specific details and perhaps a brief description of some of the skills I developed while working there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They need it by the end of the week if that's alright. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm volunteering in your area.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will write it up today. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll e-mail it to you.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Writing a Reference Letter", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You write a <span class=\"strong\">reference letter</span> (or <span class=\"strong\">recommendation letter</span>) for someone applying for a job. Primarily, a reference letter is used to introduce a person and vouch for their integrity, character, and abilities.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Your reference letter should look professional. Don't make it too long.<br/> Employers generally prefer that a reference letter fits on one page. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A reference letter should ...<ul> <li>be professional looking and sounding both in style and in format.</li> <li>not be too long or too brief as to not include enough valuable information.</li> <li>explain how you know the subject and how long you have known each other.</li> <li>be full of specific examples of the subject's work history and use of skills.</li> <li>list your own contact information if you are willing to receive follow-up correspondence or answer questions.</li> <li>have a strong ending usually recommending the subject for the new position.</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you write a reference letter, try and emphasize the positive and omit the negative.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "albeit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "although ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(conjunction)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I found Kristi to be a great asset to the organization, albeit a newer addition to the staff. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when writing a recommendation letter.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "collaborative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "willing to work with others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's an affable and highly collaborative employee.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "diligent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "hard-working ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I offer my highest recommendation for Kristi as an excellent copywriter, a dedicated professional, and a diligent employee.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "impeccable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "faultless", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I found Kristi's writing skills to be impeccable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "no-brainer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "requiring no debate ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In my opinion, hiring Kristi would be a no-brainer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and find a job listing you think would be suitable for a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you cannot find one then create one.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of reasons why your friend would be suitable for that job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a reference letter including how you know your friend, and specific details about their character, skills and experiences necessary to do the job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your reference aloud to a partner and ask for feedback.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I identify a potential job opportunity online for a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a letter of reference that includes how I know my friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give reasons why s/he is suitable for the job and specific examples of skills s/he has.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback to my partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}